<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35187" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-mădesco</span></b> , dŭi,
		3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch.
				n.</i>, <i>to become thoroughly wet</i>, <i>quite moist.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quasi hibernis pluviis terra permaduerit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col. 2,
					4</span></i>
			; Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 10,
			1010.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to grow soft</i> or
				<i>effeminate</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deliciis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 20, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fugite enervatam felicitatem, quā
					animi permadescunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Prov. 4, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
